WEBVTT

00:03.830 --> 00:06.400
You and Jonas, all of you, get out.

00:06.670 --> 00:08.170
But, Mister Radcliffe, that's—

00:08.170 --> 00:09.210
Get out!

00:10.500 --> 00:12.520
I really made a mess this time.

00:13.640 --> 00:14.360
Anne.

00:15.430 --> 00:18.080
I'm sorry things turned out this way.

00:18.080 --> 00:20.140
Kieth, you have nothing to apologize about.

00:20.140 --> 00:22.070
I'm grateful to you.

00:22.760 --> 00:24.780
We won't let it end this way.

00:24.780 --> 00:28.040
We'll find a way to show that 
Sammy was behind everything.

00:28.040 --> 00:31.510
Don't worry. We won't just 
wring our hands and give up.

00:33.120 --> 00:36.110
Then, Kieth, I'll see you tomorrow 
at the Exhibition.

00:36.110 --> 00:37.580
I'm looking forward to it.

00:45.110 --> 00:46.580
<i>Miss Bridget...</i>

01:03.430 --> 01:11.450
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

01:18.140 --> 01:20.870
<i>It's all right</i>

01:20.870 --> 01:24.710
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

01:24.710 --> 01:31.210
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

01:31.210 --> 01:37.780
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

01:37.780 --> 01:47.110
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

01:47.540 --> 01:50.750
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

01:50.750 --> 01:53.880
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

01:54.170 --> 02:01.000
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

02:01.000 --> 02:03.680
<i>That miracle</i>

02:03.930 --> 02:10.650
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

02:10.650 --> 02:16.940
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

02:16.940 --> 02:24.080
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

02:24.080 --> 02:32.310
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

02:33.680 --> 02:36.210
Well, it sounds like you've had 
a terrible time of it again.

02:36.570 --> 02:40.040
And it seems that there are horrible 
people in the Radcliffe school, too.

02:40.040 --> 02:42.810
Tomorrow, at the Exhibition, 
you show them what you can do!

02:42.810 --> 02:44.350
Thank you, ma'a—

02:51.040 --> 02:51.940
Jonas!

02:54.150 --> 02:56.310
What? Do you need something from me?

02:56.840 --> 02:59.120
Thank you for saving me.

02:59.120 --> 03:01.850
I-It's not like I did it for you.

03:02.710 --> 03:05.160
I just... got scared, that's all.

03:05.480 --> 03:07.120
Even so, I'm grateful to you.

03:07.450 --> 03:09.720
I'm telling you, I was <i>scared</i>! That's all!

03:09.720 --> 03:11.960
I <i>hate</i> you more than anything!

03:14.400 --> 03:16.670
What will you do now, Jonas?

03:16.960 --> 03:18.820
That's none of your business.

03:31.590 --> 03:33.850
I found the motif for my piece.

03:34.190 --> 03:37.120
Kieth complimented my sugar confection!

03:37.120 --> 03:39.070
Being praised by someone so skilled...

03:39.070 --> 03:40.700
of course I'm happy!

03:42.080 --> 03:43.660
<i>She was so excited.</i>

03:44.320 --> 03:46.120
<i>If yesterday's events hadn't happened...</i>

03:46.770 --> 03:49.120
<i>that might have been a place 
where you could have belonged.</i>

03:50.470 --> 03:51.320
<i>But...</i>

03:51.740 --> 03:55.080
<i>having you here like this 
now sets me at ease.</i>

03:56.520 --> 03:57.700
<i>It's selfish of me.</i>

03:59.410 --> 04:00.700
Challe fenn Challe!

04:00.700 --> 04:04.300
Will you hear what I have to say? 
It's a serious conversation!

04:04.300 --> 04:07.720
I told you, I will not listen to your 
serious questions anymore.

04:08.060 --> 04:11.400
Wait! This time it really is serious!

04:12.080 --> 04:15.110
Anne's silver sugar... is wrong!

04:15.110 --> 04:15.940
Wrong?

04:16.550 --> 04:18.060
I was sneaking a taste...

04:18.060 --> 04:20.780
No! I was taste-testing, just in case!

04:20.780 --> 04:24.350
And it was wrong. 
Both the flavor and the taste!

04:24.350 --> 04:26.380
That isn't Anne's silver sugar.

04:26.380 --> 04:29.120
It's the mass-produced sugar they 
made at the Radcliffe Workshop!

04:37.350 --> 04:39.210
Mithril Lid Pod.

04:39.210 --> 04:41.160
Keep this matter a secret from Anne.

04:41.160 --> 04:43.660
Don't say anything and have her 
enter the Exhibition tomorrow.

04:43.660 --> 04:45.420
Understand? Make sure of it.

04:45.990 --> 04:47.550
What are you going to do?

04:48.210 --> 04:49.930
I'll find her silver sugar.

04:53.900 --> 04:56.280
Elliott! It's me! Open up!

04:56.280 --> 04:59.820
I'm in the middle of something right now! 
Could you come back later?

05:00.200 --> 05:02.060
Let's look, just the three of us.

05:02.060 --> 05:04.650
To think they'd switch out her silver sugar.

05:04.650 --> 05:06.660
No matter how I think about it, 
it must have been...

05:06.990 --> 05:09.240
If what Challe says is true,

05:09.240 --> 05:11.740
then we'll need a witness 
or evidence to prove it.

05:11.740 --> 05:14.910
That's why we need this guy 
with his gift of gab to help us.

05:15.320 --> 05:18.630
Open up, Elliott! It's about Anne Halford!

05:21.000 --> 05:23.020
Don't say that name right now!

05:23.020 --> 05:23.800
Huh?

05:23.800 --> 05:26.010
Anne? That girl again?

05:26.760 --> 05:29.880
Did something happen? Is that why Kat's here?

05:30.660 --> 05:34.280
It must be so nice to have everyone 
fawning over you and protecting you.

05:34.280 --> 05:36.970
All that babying 
went to her head. That's why...

05:36.970 --> 05:38.660
What do you know?

05:39.600 --> 05:41.280
Y-You're...

05:41.280 --> 05:43.420
She's gotten this far all alone.

05:43.420 --> 05:45.630
No matter what happened, she never gave up.

05:45.630 --> 05:47.050
That's all.

05:47.050 --> 05:48.360
The one who has been babied...

05:48.800 --> 05:49.740
is you.

05:55.080 --> 05:56.080
So...

05:56.080 --> 05:58.730
Now that you've undone the work I did

05:58.730 --> 06:00.960
keeping her company 
as she drank away her heartbreak,

06:00.960 --> 06:02.190
what are you here to talk about?

06:02.190 --> 06:04.320
The silver sugar that Anne refined...

06:04.320 --> 06:07.010
seems to have been switched out 
for the mass-produced product.

06:07.360 --> 06:08.490
What?

06:08.490 --> 06:11.180
Who would do something so petty?

06:11.530 --> 06:14.890
We have an idea, but we need proof.

06:15.290 --> 06:16.980
Even the samllest clue would do.

06:16.980 --> 06:18.300
Wait.

06:18.300 --> 06:21.980
By "evidence," do you mean Anne's 
silver sugar that was swapped out?

06:21.980 --> 06:24.190
That sort of thing just wouldn't exist.

06:25.550 --> 06:27.350
You'd throw it away, wouldn't you?

06:27.350 --> 06:29.290
Because you did something bad.

06:29.290 --> 06:32.120
If I were the culprit, 
I'd definitely have gotten rid of it.

06:34.760 --> 06:36.680
Then, how will we...

06:36.680 --> 06:37.560
I saw it.

06:40.000 --> 06:41.550
I saw everything.

06:41.550 --> 06:47.470
Who the culprit is, what they did, 
and what happened to that girl's silver sugar.

06:47.470 --> 06:48.700
Is that true?

06:48.700 --> 06:49.840
It's true.

06:50.110 --> 06:51.240
Answer me.

06:51.240 --> 06:52.840
Who did this?

06:52.840 --> 06:54.100
What happened to the silver sugar?

06:55.920 --> 06:57.810
I have no intention of telling you.

07:04.810 --> 07:08.040
Mithril Lid Pod, is it really true?

07:08.040 --> 07:10.320
Huh? I-Is what true?

07:10.320 --> 07:11.470
About Challe.

07:11.470 --> 07:13.180
That his hiccups wouldn't stop,

07:13.180 --> 07:15.450
so he went to the outskirts 
of the city to get medicine.

07:16.320 --> 07:20.370
F-Fairies sometimes come down 
with hiccup sickness!

07:22.920 --> 07:24.500
<i>What's wrong, Challe?</i>

07:24.910 --> 07:27.250
<i>What could have happened?</i>

07:32.380 --> 07:35.480
I'm sorry, Anne. 
We might not make it in time.

07:35.480 --> 07:37.470
She just won't talk to us.

07:39.200 --> 07:41.690
Mister Hingley came with me,

07:41.690 --> 07:43.990
but Challe stayed to try to convince her.

07:44.460 --> 07:45.870
It's so frustrating.

07:45.870 --> 07:49.280
I never imagined that the Exhibition 
where I competed with you would turn into this.

07:49.880 --> 07:53.660
Wait. Kieth, you've been 
with Challe until now?

07:53.660 --> 07:54.620
What is going on?

07:55.080 --> 07:56.450
You don't know?

07:56.760 --> 07:59.590
Kieth Powell, stay in your designated area.

08:06.430 --> 08:10.120
This morning, I received this letter.

08:10.600 --> 08:11.960
This is what is written here.

08:13.400 --> 08:18.160
Anne Halford, who means to participate in 
today's Sugar Confectionary Exhibition,

08:18.160 --> 08:21.350
is not someone who is worthy of 
the title of sugar artisan.

08:21.350 --> 08:22.230
<i>What?</i>

08:23.230 --> 08:26.400
She does not possess the technical skill 
necessary to process silver sugar.

08:26.400 --> 08:29.860
As proof of this, 
the silver sugar she has brought...

08:30.220 --> 08:35.690
is the mass-produced product refined via 
special measures due to this year's poor crop.

08:37.880 --> 08:39.370
That is ridiculous!

08:39.370 --> 08:43.210
Silver Sugar Viscount, you know 
Anne's true abilities better than anyone!

08:43.210 --> 08:46.300
Do not venture your opinion 
when it isn't asked for, Kieth Powell!

08:47.420 --> 08:49.200
Since the complaint has been made,

08:49.200 --> 08:52.380
we must investigate or else risk it 
developing into future problems.

08:52.380 --> 08:54.140
As he says.

08:54.140 --> 08:58.510
Anne Halford, we will inspect the contents 
of your barrels. Do you understand?

08:58.830 --> 09:00.470
I have no objections. Please do.

09:02.700 --> 09:04.390
For the sake of accuracy,

09:04.680 --> 09:07.150
the master of the Radcliffe Workshop 
school, Marcus Radcliffe, and I...

09:07.150 --> 09:09.940
will conduct the examination together.

09:10.430 --> 09:12.040
I will remove the lid.

09:27.560 --> 09:33.590
This is the mass-produced silver sugar refined 
at the main Radcliffe workshop this year.

09:33.960 --> 09:35.030
Are you certain?

09:38.440 --> 09:39.740
<i>Why?</i>

09:50.220 --> 09:51.720
It's the mail!

09:51.720 --> 09:53.680
It could be from Millsfield!

09:53.680 --> 09:54.750
I'll go get it.

09:54.750 --> 09:57.500
Bridget, you have a nice chat 
with him, all right?

09:57.500 --> 09:58.490
Bye!

10:01.200 --> 10:02.950
I will ask just once more.

10:03.390 --> 10:04.950
What happened to the silver sugar?

10:06.730 --> 10:07.790
Answer me.

10:07.790 --> 10:10.000
If you don't, I will cut you down.

10:11.250 --> 10:13.030
That would work too.

10:13.030 --> 10:15.680
That girl would never be able to 
become a silver sugar master,

10:15.680 --> 10:19.210
and you'd be disposed of 
as a fairy who killed a human.

10:19.840 --> 10:22.220
You could never go back to her.

10:22.690 --> 10:24.310
It would be a lovers' suicide with me.

10:35.990 --> 10:38.700
Do you still want my wing?

10:40.870 --> 10:41.950
I do.

10:42.270 --> 10:45.450
Would you tell me everything 
in exchange for it?

10:45.900 --> 10:46.580
Yes.

10:54.520 --> 10:55.460
Tell me.

10:57.330 --> 10:58.820
Your wing.

11:05.620 --> 11:06.890
Kiss me.

11:09.440 --> 11:11.100
What? Wait, I...

11:29.330 --> 11:31.880
I know where the silver sugar is.

11:34.040 --> 11:37.250
What is the meaning of this, Anne Halford?

11:38.210 --> 11:39.720
I don't know.

11:40.120 --> 11:45.010
But I did refine the silver sugar with my own 
hands and used it to make my piece.

11:45.010 --> 11:46.110
Disqualify her!

11:46.110 --> 11:48.850
If she didn't refine the silver sugar 
herself, then she's not qualified!

11:48.220 --> 11:50.360
That's right! It's not fair!

11:50.360 --> 11:53.520
You impetuous louts! 
Despite how it looks, Anne Halford is—

11:53.850 --> 11:57.320
She's the artisan who made a sugar 
confection for the former Duke of Philax!

11:57.320 --> 12:01.490
I know this! It's impossible that she'd be 
unable to make silver sugar herself!

12:01.490 --> 12:03.950
We won't stand for this! Disqualify her!

12:04.300 --> 12:05.720
Silence!

12:05.720 --> 12:08.290
Our king, His Majesty Edmond II, approaches!

12:12.760 --> 12:15.370
What is this commotion, Downing?

12:23.920 --> 12:25.290
You again?

12:25.290 --> 12:28.760
After last year, it seems you 
enjoy creating utter turmoil.

12:29.070 --> 12:31.730
My deepest apologies, sire. I only...

12:32.090 --> 12:33.870
I have heard the story.

12:33.870 --> 12:35.200
Regardless of the reason,

12:35.200 --> 12:38.220
as someone without silver sugar 
you have processed yourself,

12:38.220 --> 12:39.820
you are not qualified to stand here.

12:55.160 --> 12:57.830
Before you go, show us your piece.

12:59.480 --> 13:02.330
Not as an entry in the Exhibition, of course.

13:02.800 --> 13:04.020
We simply wish to see it.

13:04.630 --> 13:06.260
My queen has said so.

13:29.200 --> 13:30.620
It's exquisite.

13:33.220 --> 13:37.960
Your Majesty! Is there a fairy upon whom 
you have bestowed your trust?

13:38.400 --> 13:39.420
A fairy?

13:41.220 --> 13:42.460
Clifford!

13:42.460 --> 13:43.170
Come here.

13:45.460 --> 13:47.420
I would trust him.

13:47.420 --> 13:48.840
Thank you, sire.

13:52.430 --> 13:53.390
Anne?

13:56.080 --> 13:59.670
I've heard that fairies can taste 
the differences in silver sugar.

14:00.120 --> 14:04.150
And they'd be able to tell 
what silver sugar this confection is made of.

14:04.720 --> 14:06.660
I am giving this to you.

14:07.730 --> 14:08.820
Are you sure?

14:08.820 --> 14:10.910
I hope it suits your tastes.

14:12.290 --> 14:13.240
In that case...

14:29.040 --> 14:30.590
It was delicious. Incredibly so.

14:32.680 --> 14:36.190
This is made from 
a very high-quality silver sugar.

14:36.190 --> 14:38.440
It is completely different 
from a mass-produced product.

14:38.440 --> 14:39.900
That can't be!

14:40.440 --> 14:43.370
To go so far as to sacrifice 
the piece she labored so hard upon...

14:43.370 --> 14:44.980
Has she proven her innocence?

14:44.980 --> 14:48.820
I created my piece from my silver sugar.

14:49.450 --> 14:51.590
That is the one thing 
I hope people will understand.

14:52.260 --> 14:56.670
For twice disrupting the sacred 
Sugar Confectionary Exhibition...

14:56.670 --> 14:58.730
I offer my deepest apologies, 
from the bottom of my heart.

15:02.960 --> 15:05.990
<i>Challe! Miss Bridget...</i>

15:07.080 --> 15:10.960
The daughter of Glen Paige, master of 
the Paige Workshop schools, is here.

15:10.960 --> 15:13.520
Your Majesty, she says she has 
something she wishes to tell you.

15:13.520 --> 15:14.180
Let her pass.

15:16.150 --> 15:19.690
I am Glen Paige's daughter. 
My name is Bridget.

15:19.690 --> 15:20.700
What brings you here?

15:21.370 --> 15:22.470
I...

15:22.940 --> 15:24.840
know the artisan in attendance here,

15:24.840 --> 15:28.530
Anne Halford, and I know the whereabouts 
of the silver sugar she refined.

15:35.470 --> 15:38.410
Indeed? Then, where is it?

15:39.190 --> 15:40.080
There.

15:40.760 --> 15:44.540
In there, there should be barrels 
with the name Sammy Jones written on them.

15:44.920 --> 15:48.920
But the barrels are not filled 
with silver sugar which he has refined.

15:49.520 --> 15:51.510
It's Anne Halford's silver sugar.

15:51.510 --> 15:52.720
What did you say?

15:53.230 --> 15:54.830
I'm sorry, Sammy.

15:54.830 --> 15:56.540
I saw everything.

15:56.540 --> 16:00.570
I saw you and your friends 
carrying barrels out of Anne's cart.

16:01.000 --> 16:04.060
I hadn't planned on saying anything, 
but circumstances have changed.

16:04.400 --> 16:07.290
That can't be! It's just a false accusation 
from the Paige school!

16:07.290 --> 16:09.530
Right, Sammy? Tell them I'm right!

16:10.100 --> 16:12.860
Bring Sammy Jones' silver sugar here!

16:17.800 --> 16:19.480
It's the same flavor.

16:19.480 --> 16:22.620
This is, without a doubt, 
Anne Halford's silver sugar.

16:22.970 --> 16:25.310
You switched the contents?

16:25.310 --> 16:27.660
Why? Why would you do something like that?

16:27.660 --> 16:30.090
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! Please forgive me!

16:30.500 --> 16:32.670
Why would you do that now, for this event?

16:33.460 --> 16:34.930
This silver sugar...

16:35.600 --> 16:40.100
I just thought that everything 
would be better if I'd made it.

16:42.440 --> 16:44.690
You... You...

16:44.690 --> 16:46.360
You incredible fool!

16:47.780 --> 16:51.990
Well, I suppose this is what you might call 
the nature of sugar artisans.

16:52.490 --> 16:56.170
Your Majesty, I do not know how to 
apologize for such disgraceful behavior.

16:56.170 --> 17:00.460
As master of the school, I shall take 
full responsibility and deal with him,

17:00.460 --> 17:02.910
so please! If you could 
please see your way to...

17:02.910 --> 17:05.120
This is unseemly. Leave, immediately.

17:05.120 --> 17:06.140
Sire!

17:06.140 --> 17:08.400
Downing, declare the Exhibition open.

17:08.400 --> 17:09.260
Yes, sire.

17:09.260 --> 17:10.250
Anne Halford!

17:10.640 --> 17:11.340
Yes?

17:11.630 --> 17:15.130
You have already brought your piece 
and your silver sugar here.

17:15.610 --> 17:17.280
There is no reason for you 
to leave this place.

17:17.280 --> 17:19.280
Oh! Y-Yes, sire!

17:22.160 --> 17:24.760
Thank you, Miss Bridget.

17:24.760 --> 17:27.980
No need for that. 
I've already received my thanks.

17:36.190 --> 17:39.740
We now declare 
the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition open!

17:39.740 --> 17:43.210
The greatest sugar artisan in the kingdom...

17:43.210 --> 17:46.830
shall be granted the title of 
Silver Sugar Master. This we promise you.

17:46.830 --> 17:51.210
Citizens, His Majesty will now 
look upon the sugar confections.

17:59.590 --> 18:02.750
What a powerful, elegant fairy.

18:02.750 --> 18:06.770
This is what is meant by 
the phrase "utterly flawless."

18:07.270 --> 18:09.720
The way the sugar confection 
gives form to the fairy...

18:09.720 --> 18:11.770
I've never seen better.

18:12.790 --> 18:15.900
Downing, what is this artisan's name?

18:15.900 --> 18:17.400
Kieth Powell.

18:17.400 --> 18:20.590
He is the son of the previous 
Silver Sugar Viscount.

18:20.590 --> 18:22.460
I see. A blood relative, then?

18:23.220 --> 18:24.590
Kieth Powell.

18:24.590 --> 18:25.200
Yes, sire.

18:25.710 --> 18:28.640
You inherited your father's 
sensitivity and craftsmanship.

18:28.640 --> 18:30.920
Your sugar confection is perfect.

18:31.650 --> 18:34.220
As a piece which imitates this world of ours,

18:34.220 --> 18:35.510
I can say it is the best.

18:38.950 --> 18:42.180
As a piece which imitates this world.

18:43.190 --> 18:45.640
I see! That's why I...

18:45.960 --> 18:47.870
No matter how detailed it may be,

18:47.870 --> 18:51.060
nothing created by man can compare 
to the beauty of the real thing.

18:51.990 --> 18:54.610
In contrast, Anne Halford's piece...

18:54.970 --> 18:58.640
a fairy wing woven together 
with climbing roses.

18:58.640 --> 19:02.500
She has given form to something 
which can only be described as a vision.

19:03.200 --> 19:06.470
Even the scar left by 
the flower she broke off...

19:06.470 --> 19:08.410
looks beautiful to me.

19:09.640 --> 19:11.370
I understand, sire.

19:15.580 --> 19:17.350
I will now make a declaration!

19:17.350 --> 19:20.350
Anne Halford's sugar confection...

19:20.350 --> 19:23.110
shall be awarded this year's Royal Medal.

19:23.510 --> 19:27.140
And the one who made this piece, 
is this year's Silver Sugar Master!

19:30.590 --> 19:34.690
You did it! Anne! It's the Royal Medal!

19:34.690 --> 19:35.800
You did it!

19:35.000 --> 19:38.230
Go on, Anne. His Majesty 
and the others are waiting for you.

19:35.800 --> 19:37.790
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

19:37.790 --> 19:41.320
Yay! Yay! Yay!

19:38.230 --> 19:40.650
Me? The Royal Medal?

19:41.040 --> 19:43.870
Come on, Miss Novice Silver Sugar Master.

19:45.820 --> 19:46.800
For the rest of your days...

19:46.800 --> 19:50.950
live in reverence of the sacred 
as a maker of the sacred.

19:58.120 --> 19:59.100
<i>Mama.</i>

20:03.140 --> 20:04.510
I will live!

20:04.510 --> 20:07.220
I will live as a maker of the sacred 
for the rest of my days!

20:12.570 --> 20:14.350
I am an idiot.

20:14.350 --> 20:16.980
It wasn't the time for me 
to be worrying about you.

20:17.520 --> 20:20.150
But next year, I will receive it too.

20:20.560 --> 20:22.700
When I do, let's compete again.

20:22.700 --> 20:23.500
Yes!

20:23.990 --> 20:25.560
Um, Kieth...

20:26.750 --> 20:28.000
Thank you.

20:28.000 --> 20:30.660
Because you were there for me, 
I was able to keep trying.

20:30.660 --> 20:33.120
You're thanking the wrong person.

20:33.680 --> 20:36.360
The one who convinced Bridget was Challe.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.880
You have to hurry up and show him that medal.

20:38.880 --> 20:41.980
Yes! Then, Kieth... I'll see you again!

20:43.460 --> 20:44.500
Challe!

20:45.550 --> 20:47.760
Look! It's the Royal Medal!

20:50.500 --> 20:52.620
You've managed to take hold of your future.

20:53.280 --> 20:54.180
You...

20:55.760 --> 20:57.320
no longer need me.

20:57.320 --> 20:58.110
What?

20:58.690 --> 21:00.570
Wait, Challe. What are you saying?

21:02.000 --> 21:04.780
I can't stay with you anymore.

21:05.800 --> 21:07.130
What do you mean?

21:07.580 --> 21:10.440
Did you get tired of being with me?

21:11.980 --> 21:14.210
Challe... Challe, what—

21:24.120 --> 21:25.550
I didn't want to let go.

21:35.380 --> 21:36.920
Why...

21:37.440 --> 21:41.710
Well, this isn't good. A girl shouldn't be 
sitting in a place like this.

21:41.710 --> 21:43.220
Your dress will get dirty.

21:43.960 --> 21:45.280
Mister Collins?

21:45.600 --> 21:48.620
Not knowing causes you sorrow, doesn't it?

21:48.620 --> 21:51.830
Since I am the ally 
of all women, I will tell you.

21:52.680 --> 21:57.310
In order to make her tell him 
where your silver sugar was, that fairy...

21:57.310 --> 21:59.500
gave his wing to Bridget.

21:59.990 --> 22:01.180
His wing?

22:01.180 --> 22:01.900
Yes.

22:02.420 --> 22:05.540
For your sake, he sold his freedom.

22:07.950 --> 22:08.800
<i>Wait.</i>

22:09.400 --> 22:10.860
<i>Challe, you can't.</i>

22:11.260 --> 22:13.220
<i>Please, wait!</i>

22:17.140 --> 22:19.780
<i>Challe. Challe!</i>

22:19.780 --> 22:21.860
<i>Please! Don't go!</i>

22:26.080 --> 22:29.030
Challe!

22:29.120 --> 22:35.040
I Didn't Want to Let Go
